(text "MDBT50Q-P1MV2 (nRF52840, PCB antenna). 32 MHz crystal and the radio DC/DC inductor are inside the module.\nREG0 DC/DC is on: VBAT to VDDH, 10 uH from DCCH to VDD, 10 uF on VDDH and on VDD (Raytac section 8.1, L4 = 10 uH).\nUSB is unused. D+ and D- are open. VBUS is tied to GND.\nNFC1 and NFC2 are open. Keep copper off every layer under the antenna end and place that end at the board edge.\nQSPI uses the module pins Raytac marks for QSPI: P0.19 SCK, P0.20 IO0, P0.21 IO1, P0.22 IO2, P0.23 IO3, P0.17 CS.\nnRESET is P0.18 (module pin 40), so chip-select is P0.17 and not P0.18.\nY1 is optional. Raytac says to delete the crystal and its load caps when the internal 32.768 kHz RC is used.\nPins not named here are no-connect, including the low-frequency-only GPIOs that are not used." (at 40 250 0)
  (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)))
  (uuid 6195e791-0f00-43f4-b87e-4a14e39ce233)
)

  (sheet_instances (path "/a1b2c3d4-1111-4111-8111-111111111111/c1b2c3d4-3333-4333-8333-333333333333" (page "3")))
)
